{%- comment -%}
  PG Upsell Fit: the in-cart offer rows state the offer in full on a phone.

  ------------------------------------------------------------ WHAT WAS WRONG

  On an iPhone 13 / 16 / 17 (390-402pt) the pg-unlock offer rows read

      "Add a 2nd PocketB..."          instead of  "Add a 2nd R36S"
      "Unlock Buy 2, Get 1 ..."       instead of  "Unlock Buy 2, Get 1 FREE"
      "SAVE 25" / "SAVE 5"            instead of  "SAVE 25%" / "SAVE 50%"

  -- the headline cut off mid-word and the discount chip cut off mid-number,
  with its tail painted under the ADD button. Both come from the same squeeze.

  THE SQUEEZE. screen.css styles every bare <button> with

      button { min-width: var(--btn_miw); }        /* min(100%, 120px) here */

  so the three-letter ADD button takes 120px. The drawer is the full viewport
  on a phone (pg-drawer) less var(--rpp) either side, so at 390pt the row has
  358px of content: 120px button + 46px thumbnail + gaps + card padding leaves
  the copy column about 154px. pg-unlock never waives that min-width, and no
  amount of padding tuning can go under it.

  WHAT THE COLUMN THEN DID WITH 154px. pg-cart-tune styles this row at four
  ids and, measured at 390/393/414/430 when it was written, both of its
  choices were safe there and are not here:

    - the title was `white-space:nowrap; text-overflow:ellipsis`, which is only
      safe while the column is wider than the longest title;
    - the price line was `flex-wrap:nowrap` with the SAVE chip at
      `flex:0 1 auto; min-width:0`. When that line cannot fit and cannot break,
      the one item allowed to shrink is the only thing that can give -- and a
      shrunken inline-block with nowrap text simply clips. A misstated discount
      is worse than a wrapped one.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ THE FIX

  Three declarations, at FIVE ids so they win over pg-cart-tune's four (and
  pg-cart-timer's two, and pg-unlock's three) at any load order -- which also
  means a theme-editor reorder of the section groups cannot unseat them:

    1. the ADD button waives --btn_miw and is sized by its own padding
       (~55px), handing ~65px back to the copy;
    2. the title wraps, to at most two lines, and is never ellipsised;
    3. the price line wraps and the SAVE chip never shrinks -- whole badge on
       the price line where it fits, whole badge on its own line where it does
       not.

  Measured in Chromium against the real markup and the real stylesheets at
  375/390/393/402/414/430/485: no truncated title, no clipped chip, no row
  overflow, and the chip ends 65-154px clear of the ADD button.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- THE NAME

  The console is the R36S. "PocketBoy R36" is an older name for it and is
  still hardcoded in two places the shopper reads inside the drawer:
  pg-unlock's LADDERS (the offer headline) and pg-drawer's pgBar (the
  free-case progress message). Both files are 54-64KB and can only be written
  whole, so the name is corrected here in the drawer's text nodes instead --
  the same approach pg-cart-mobile already takes for the "PokeOrb" rename, and
  for the same reason.

  It cannot flicker: pg-unlock rewrites a row wholesale (so this re-runs after
  it and then finds nothing), and pg-drawer's message writer is guarded on
  data-m -- what IT last wrote -- not on what the node currently says, so it
  does not write back over this. Idempotent either way.

  WHEN pg-unlock OR pg-drawer IS NEXT REDEPLOYED CLEAN, fix the strings at
  source (`name: 'R36S'` in pg-unlock's LADDERS; the two `<b>PocketBoy R36</b>`
  literals in pg-drawer's pgBar) and this sweep quietly finds nothing to do.
  The cart PAGE's copy of the name is already fixed at source, in
  pg-cart-upsell.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the ADD button waives the theme's 120px floor: it is three letters */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock-add{min-width:0 !important}

  /* the headline is never truncated; two lines at most */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock-t b{
    white-space:normal !important;
    text-overflow:clip !important;
    overflow-wrap:break-word !important;
    overflow:hidden !important;
    display:-webkit-box !important;
    -webkit-box-orient:vertical !important;
    -webkit-line-clamp:2 !important;
  }

  /* the price line may wrap, and the SAVE chip is whole or nothing */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock-px{
    flex-wrap:wrap !important;
    gap:2px 6px !important;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock-px .pg-unlock-tag{
    flex:0 0 auto !important;
    min-width:auto !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }

  /* same rule for the accessory tickbox under the row: it is a sentence, and
     at 11px in a column this narrow it was one ellipsis away from the same
     problem */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-uacc-t{
    white-space:normal !important;
    overflow:visible !important;
    text-overflow:clip !important;
    line-height:1.3 !important;
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgUpsellFit) return; window.pgUpsellFit = 1;

  var OLD = 'PocketBoy', RE = /PocketBoy\s+R36S?/g;

  function sweep(){
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!c || c.textContent.indexOf(OLD) === -1) return;
    var w = document.createTreeWalker(c, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT, null), n, hits = [];
    while ((n = w.nextNode())){ if (n.nodeValue.indexOf(OLD) > -1) hits.push(n); }
    hits.forEach(function(t){ t.nodeValue = t.nodeValue.replace(RE, 'R36S'); });
  }

  function boot(){
    sweep();
    /* the drawer is rebuilt on every cart change by several writers, so the
       rename rides on the mutations rather than on a timer of its own;
       debounced, and the textContent check above makes a no-op pass cheap */
    if (!window.MutationObserver) return;
    var q = false;
    new MutationObserver(function(){
      if (q) return;
      q = true;
      setTimeout(function(){ q = false; sweep(); }, 60);
    }).observe(document.documentElement, {childList: true, subtree: true, characterData: true});
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Upsell Fit", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
